sec.p:
The information extracted for each record included: author(s); year of publication; country of origin; aims/purpose of the study; population; study design; type of sleep measurement; sampling cortisol; sampling timing; association between salivary cortisol and sleep quality and key findings. Details are described below:
Author(s): author or authors who conducted the study;
Year of publication: year in which the document/record was published;
Country: country associated with the corresponding author of the publication;
Aim(s) of the study: overall aim(s) and main objective(s) of the publication;
Population: type of sample recruited for the study;
Study design: cross-sectional, longitudinal, randomized controlled trial, non-randomized controlled trial, cohort study, etc.;
Sleep measurement: subjective or objective assessment or both, and which tools were used to collect the data;
Cortisol sampling: collection method, storage condition, timing, frequency, and cortisol detection assay;
Key findings: correlation between sleep outcome and cortisol level.
